        <h1>Exercise Name: Seated Incline Dumbbell Bicep Curl</h1>
        <u><h4><b>Exercise Overview</b></h4></u>


This 3D anatomical visualization demonstrates Seated Incline Dumbbell Bicep Curls. The video highlights the biceps (Biceps Brachii — especially the long head) in bright glowing colors, illustrating how sitting back on an inclined bench stretches the bicep at the starting position to maximize muscle engagement throughout the curl.
 Exercise Name: Seated Incline Dumbbell Bicep Curl
 Target Muscles: Biceps (Biceps Brachii — with emphasis on the Long Head)
 Secondary Muscles: Brachialis, Forearm Flexors
</div></div>
<pre>
<h1>

How to Perform (Step-by-Step)</h1> <u><h4><b>1.Setup</b></h4></u>
 Set an adjustable workout bench to a 45 to 60-degree incline. Sit back with your head and back firmly pressed against the pad, holding a dumbbell in each hand. Let your arms hang straight down behind your torso with palms facing forward.
 <u><h4><b>2.Curling Phase</b></h4></u>
 Keep your upper arms stationary and back flat against the pad. Exhale as you curl both dumbbells upward toward your shoulders, rotating your palms slightly outward (supinating) if needed.
 <u><h4><b>3.Peak Squeeze</b></h4></u>
 Pause for a split second at top position to contract your biceps tightly.
 <u><h4><b>4.Lowering Phase</b></h4></u>
 Inhale as you slowly lower the dumbbells back down under control over 2 to 3 seconds until your arms are fully extended and you feel a deep stretch in your biceps.



<h1>Key Benefits</h1>

 <b>◉Maximizes Bicep Stretch:</b> The inclined position places the long head of the bicep under a deep stretch, which is proven to stimulate greater muscle hypertrophy (growth).
 <b>◉Eliminates Cheating:</b> Leaning back against the bench prevents you from using torso momentum or swinging your body to lift the weights.
 <b>◉  Builds Bicep Peak:</b> Target loading on the long head directly contributes to creating a taller, more defined bicep peak.


<h1>Recommended Sets & Reps</h1>

| Goal | Sets | Reps | Rest |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Muscle Building (Hypertrophy) | 3 – 4 | 10 – 12 | 60 – 90 seconds |
| Endurance / Tone | 3 – 4 | 12 – 15 | 45 – 60 seconds |
| Strength | 3 – 4 | 8 – 10 | 90 seconds |

Keep your elbows stationary and back against the bench—do not let your elbows drift forward as you lift the weights.
